{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/887763-questions-after-tonight-s-session","id":887763,"title":"Questions after tonight's session","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-10T19:38:40-07:00","id":887763,"title":"Questions after tonight's session","content":"Some from my players and some from me. So prime mage sight will show the mage anything that can be used as a yantra. But in theory, anything can be used as a yantra, so I'm not sure I see the distinction. Is this for dedicated magical tools? (character creation mentions dedicated magical tools, but I didn't see it mention how many of these a mage may have ... for that matter, I didn't see any indication as to how many yantra a mage may have, just how many they may use in any one casting). <br /> <br /> So spells have attached suggested rote skills. Three of them. Are those just suggestions? The most common skills? Will a given rote for that ability use one or all of them? How do I decide which to use? I was pretty vague here. Someone asked and I didn't know what to tell them. <br /> <br /> Am I the only one who thinks the wording of dispel magic and supernal dispellation are identical? i see no difference. <br /> <br /> I think that's all i've got for now. We had a blast at game and I'm glad that even with half rules I've been running time travel correctly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6014-anivair","name":"Anivair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6014_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T19:48:38-07:00","id":887768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anivair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/887763-questions-after-tonight-s-session#post887763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ... for that matter, I didn't see any indication as to how many yantra a mage may have, just how many they may use in any one casting).</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure they don't track what Yantras you have outside of those being used during a casting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Am I the only one who thinks the wording of dispel magic and supernal dispellation are identical? i see no difference. </div> </div> </div>The big one: Dispel Magic requires at least a dot of each arcana involved in the casting, Supernal Dispellation only needs prime.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T19:56:45-07:00","id":887771,"title":"","content":"A mage may have one dedicated tool at one time. A mage may use a maximum number of yantras according to their gnosis in each spell. A yantra is symbolism of an item, every item contains symbolism but a mage can only utilize so many symbols at once.<br /> <br /> Your rote yantras as determined by your order. Each order gives three. So the suggested skill for spells is mostly just saying which of those skill the developers think should fit but are not the only ones that can fit. I'd say that when you learn a rote you learn it with a set rote yantra (skill) that can apply to it but I am not sure if that is how the game is intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T20:28:41-07:00","id":887787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kirby Jerusalem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/887763-questions-after-tonight-s-session?p=887768#post887768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The big one: Dispel Magic requires at least a dot of each arcana involved in the casting, Supernal Dispellation only needs prime.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh, yeah, that bit looked like it was all the flavor text, so I glossed over it. thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6014-anivair","name":"Anivair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6014_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T20:29:53-07:00","id":887788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/887763-questions-after-tonight-s-session?p=887771#post887771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A mage may have one dedicated tool at one time. A mage may use a maximum number of yantras according to their gnosis in each spell. A yantra is symbolism of an item, every item contains symbolism but a mage can only utilize so many symbols at once.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must have missed the bit about having only one dedicated tool at a time. I'll look again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6014-anivair","name":"Anivair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6014_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T20:38:15-07:00","id":887796,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;Each mage has<b> <u>a</u></b> Dedicated Magical Tool... If it gets destroyed or lost, she can replace it...she must use her chosen tool as a Yantra in every spell she casts for a month (counting against her limit), regardless of whether doing so gives any benefit...&quot; pg 123 emphasis mine</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Hope this helps. Because of the way english is structured that 'a' refers to a singular instance and the effort one has to go through to establish a new dedicated tool I feel that singular nature is supported. It'd also be strange in my opinion if you were not dedicated to a dedicated tool (having multiple dedicated tools).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T21:55:35-07:00","id":887880,"title":"","content":"You can dedicate only one tool, but you may use multiple dedicated tools. Some abilities allow you to count something as a &quot;dedicated tool&quot;. Egregore does that, Techne does that, turning something into a Soul Stone does that, Adamant Hand does that, and so on. In these cases, Dedicated Tool benefit does stack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T23:00:46-07:00","id":887912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/887763-questions-after-tonight-s-session?p=887880#post887880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can dedicate only one tool, but you may use multiple dedicated tools. Some abilities allow you to count something as a &quot;dedicated tool&quot;. Egregore does that, Techne does that, turning something into a Soul Stone does that, Adamant Hand does that, and so on. In these cases, Dedicated Tool benefit does stack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Egregor (****) and a mage using their own soul stone as a Yantra are considered using their respective items as dedicated magical tools, pp. 98, 101. <br /> <br /> However, Adamant Hand and Techne do not. Both merits permit their respective purviews to become <i>Order</i> tools (+1 bonus to spellcasting), not dedicated magical tools.<br /> <br /> It is also unclear whether the Paradox mitigation benefit provided by a mage's one officially permitted dedicated magical tool stacks with the Egregore or soul stone Yantra benefit or if the maximum Paradox mitigation for use of dedicated magical tools is -2.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T23:03:41-07:00","id":887915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/887763-questions-after-tonight-s-session?p=887880#post887880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can dedicate only one tool, but you may use multiple dedicated tools. Some abilities allow you to count something as a &amp;quot;dedicated tool&amp;quot;. Egregore does that, Techne does that, turning something into a Soul Stone does that, Adamant Hand does that, and so on. In these cases, Dedicated Tool benefit does stack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, didn't notice that thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T01:53:00-07:00","id":887991,"title":"","content":"Yantras seen with Prime should be able to determine their relative value to casting. In other words, yes, anything can be a yantra, but Prime will tell you that the plain wooden cup is a better Yantra for a healing spell than all those gold ones.<br /> <br /> The Rote skills are just typical skills that are used for encoding Rotes. A Master only encodes one skill into his Rote, so two Mages might know an identical Rote but use completely different skills to cast it. Use it to individuate your Master NPCs a bit. They're just suggestions, so feel free to figure out how any skill could have a metaphysical reason to enforce the Imago of a given spell in the forging of a Rote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 05-11-2016, 04:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T17:58:22-07:00","id":890299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/887763-questions-after-tonight-s-session?p=887796#post887796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;Each mage has<b> <u>a</u></b> Dedicated Magical Tool... If it gets destroyed or lost, she can replace it...she must use her chosen tool as a Yantra in every spell she casts for a month (counting against her limit), regardless of whether doing so gives any benefit...&quot; pg 123 emphasis mine</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Hope this helps. Because of the way english is structured that 'a' refers to a singular instance and the effort one has to go through to establish a new dedicated tool I feel that singular nature is supported. It'd also be strange in my opinion if you were not dedicated to a dedicated tool (having multiple dedicated tools).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To be fair, that's a lot to take away from the single use of an article. I hope it's clarified a bit in errata.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6014-anivair","name":"Anivair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6014_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T18:37:34-07:00","id":890324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anivair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/887763-questions-after-tonight-s-session?p=890299#post890299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> To be fair, that's a lot to take away from the single use of an article. I hope it's clarified a bit in errata.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly it's more: it is called 'dedicated' + refered in the singular form + alot of effort to replace.<br /> <br /> Since the only way mentioned to have a new dedicated tool mentions it replacing the old one I am of the opinion that you can only have one true dedicated tool while some other things (your soul stone) can function as one but isn't one. <br /> <br /> Sorry if the bolded point seemed to be the only peice I was presenting to support my position but the whole quoted section was meant to. I just didn't feel like breaking down the who thing line by line. I do agree I hope it is clarified in errata or FAQ.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T20:11:47-07:00","id":988084,"title":"","content":"I too was curious if the Soul Stone was able to stack with a Dedicated Tool for paradox mitigation, but it seems post errata that's not addressed?<br /> <br /> So I guess now it will just come down to ST preferences. What preferences do some of you have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}